Most Warlocks use Voidwalkers because **Torment** provides reliable threat generation, allowing the Warlock to cast damage spells without pulling aggro and dying. While the Succubus offers higher damage, she lacks a taunt; her threat reduction (**Soothing Kiss**) can cause mobs to switch targets to the fragile Warlock, making leveling dangerous and inefficient despite the DPS loss. [end of text]


